      "content": "#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <cstdio>\n#include <cassert>\n#include <limits>\n\nint main() {\n    int n, s;\n    std::cin >> n >> s;\n    std::vector<std::vector<int> > matrix(n, std::vector<int>(n));\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i)\n        for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j)\n            scanf(\"%d\", &matrix[i][j]);\n\n    assert(s < n);\n    assert(n < 8000);\n    assert(s > 0);\n    assert(n > 0);\n\n    using Sum = long long;\n    std::vector<Sum> columns(n, 0);\n    Sum* const column = columns.data();\n\n    for (int rowIndex = 0; rowIndex < s; ++rowIndex) {\n        const int* const row = matrix[rowIndex].data();\n#if defined(__GNUC__) && !defined(__clang__)\n#pragma GCC ivdep\n#endif\n        for (int c = 0; c < n; ++c)\n            column[c] += static_cast<Sum>(row[c]);\n    }\n\n    Sum maximum = std::numeric_limits<Sum>::lowest();\n    for (int top = 0; top <= n - s; ++top) {\n        if (top != 0) {\n            const int* const leaving = matrix[top - 1].data();\n            const int* const entering = matrix[top + s - 1].data();\n#if defined(__GNUC__) && !defined(__clang__)\n#pragma GCC ivdep\n#endif\n            for (int c = 0; c < n; ++c)\n                column[c] += static_cast<Sum>(entering[c]) - leaving[c];\n        }\n\n        Sum window = 0;\n        for (int c = 0; c < s; ++c)\n            window += column[c];\n        if (window > maximum)\n            maximum = window;\n\n        for (int c = s; c < n; ++c) {\n            window += column[c] - column[c - s];\n            if (window > maximum)\n                maximum = window;\n        }\n    }\n\n    printf(\"%d\\n\", static_cast<int>(maximum));\n    return 0;\n}\n",
      "path": "src/solution.cpp"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "Maintaining contiguous vertical column sums removes repeated strided scans and exposes independent SIMD updates, reducing computation from O(SN²) to O(N²).",
